    <briefdescription>
<para>Creates KMS clients by name. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Catalogs create their KMS client from the catalog properties, with the same property names as Java:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>encryption.kms-type</computeroutput>: a built-in client, <computeroutput>aws</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>gcp</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>azure</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>encryption.kms-impl</computeroutput>: the name a custom client was registered under.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Java has no built-in clients yet and rejects every <computeroutput>encryption.kms-type</computeroutput> (EncryptionUtil.createKmsClient); here the type names resolve through the same registry, so a client registered under one of them is used.</para>
<para>Built-in clients register themselves when their library is linked and initialized; applications register custom clients before creating catalogs. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
